Z||000008||Standard||06-26-2001||01:37 AM||||kinda on topic..<P>I have a sony DVP-S560 DVD player that quit working awhile ago.. listening to a cd with it one morning, then left it on for a few hours, came back and tried to play a DVD and it wouldn't recognize the disc.  Tried cleaning the disc off, wouldn't work.  Tried different discs, leaving it on for a few days, unplugging it, etc etc..  any ideas?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/wacko.gif"> <BR>1986 GT 5 speed<BR>1984 SC Auto<P>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus||||reg||1
Z||000009||DecadenceR||06-26-2001||11:53 AM||||usually leaving DVD players on for a few hours is bad... They begin to overheat. That's one of the problems that had PS2 pushed back. You'd watch a movie adn then go to play a game on it, and it would break up on teh screen and you got premature motor failure.<BR>HOw old is the unit? From what I understand most DVD players if used heavily are only good for a few years. But if it's not that old, I'd contact the company to get it fixed or replaced.||||reg||1
